    {
      "id": "DbfLPr-KMSpKY5w46wfj1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1356.5357127982093,
      "y": 1953.2766747843712,
      "width": 1256.364990234375,
      "height": 525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bsb",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1757205788,
      "version": 373,
      "versionNonce": 168082212,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788425670817,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Employee & Contract\n\n- Employees should be viewable in both Kanban and List views.\n- Opening an employee should show their HR details and related records such as Contracts,\nAttendance, Time Off, and Allocations.\n- An employee can have multiple contracts over time.\n- Payroll should use the contract applicable to the selected payroll period.\n\nWorking Schedule\n- Working Schedules need List and Form views. Clicking a row should open that schedule.\n- List should surface name, calendar type, days/week, hours/week, company and status.\n- Form defines the weekly pattern: day, start/end time, optional break and hours. Weekly\nhours should be derived from the schedule.\n- A schedule can be assigned to an Employee/Contract and used by Attendance and Payroll.\nShift, flexible-time and other rules are open to the participant.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "iyCY-CFYgVBfZdvMZVKdm",
      "originalText": "Employee & Contract\n\n- Employees should be viewable in both Kanban and List views.\n- Opening an employee should show their HR details and related records such as Contracts,\nAttendance, Time Off, and Allocations.\n- An employee can have multiple contracts over time.\n- Payroll should use the contract applicable to the selected payroll period.\n\nWorking Schedule\n- Working Schedules need List and Form views. Clicking a row should open that schedule.\n- List should surface name, calendar type, days/week, hours/week, company and status.\n- Form defines the weekly pattern: day, start/end time, optional break and hours. Weekly\nhours should be derived from the schedule.\n- A schedule can be assigned to an Employee/Contract and used by Attendance and Payroll.\nShift, flexible-time and other rules are open to the participant.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6bUB6QuWXbFD2CvMvLS7K",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 2360.169968999411,
      "y": 3573.1165941895797,
      "width": 1400.000000000001,
      "height": 294.3452380952382,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
