      "versionNonce": 1031908388,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788425670817,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Payrun Creation:\n\nCreating a Payrun happens in two steps:\n\n- Select the payroll scope, such as employee type, salary structure, and period.\n- Select the employees to include.\n- Continue only moves to employee selection. A Payrun is created only after clicking “Create\nPayrun”.\nOnly the selected employees should be included in that Payrun.\n\n\nPayruns & Payslips:\n\nA Payrun represents payroll processing for a particular period.\nEach selected employee should have a Payslip linked to the Payrun.\nComputing payroll should use the employee’s applicable contract and selected salary structure.\nPayslips should show understandable components such as Basic, Allowances, Deductions, Gross,\nand Net Salary.\nPayroll issues, such as missing required information or duplicate payslips, should be visible to the\nuser.\n\n\nPayroll Workflow:\n\nThe intended flow is broadly:\n\nDraft → Compute → Validate → Mark Paid\n\nPaid/finalised payroll should remain available as historical data.\n\n\nSalary Structures & Salary Rules:\n\nA Salary Structure contains the rules used to calculate salary.\nSalary Rules can represent Basic Salary, Allowances, Deductions, Gross, Net, etc.\nRules should be processed according to their sequence.\nDifferent calculation methods may be supported, such as fixed amounts, percentages, or formulas.\n\nParticipants are free to design the calculation engine as long as salary rules actually drive Payslip\ncalculations.\n\n\nPayslip PDF:\n\nUsers should be able to generate/print a Payslip showing the employee’s payroll calculation for\nthat period.\nSending Payslips can also be supported from the Payrun.\n\n\nPayroll Dashboard:\n\nThe dashboard should use actual data created through the HR and Payroll flows rather than\nhardcoded values.\n\nIt should provide useful payroll/HR insights such as:\n\nSalary totals\nPayslip status\nSalary by department\nSalary trends\nAttendance overview\nTime Off overview\nPayroll warnings or items requiring attention\n\nFilters such as Period, Department, Employee Type, or Company should affect the relevant\ndashboard data.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "V8Ezd9AmXTwfauNjOHJRv",
      "originalText": "Payrun Creation:\n\nCreating a Payrun happens in two steps:\n\n- Select the payroll scope, such as employee type, salary structure, and period.\n- Select the employees to include.\n- Continue only moves to employee selection. A Payrun is created only after clicking “Create Payrun”.\nOnly the selected employees should be included in that Payrun.\n\n\nPayruns & Payslips:\n\nA Payrun represents payroll processing for a particular period.\nEach selected employee should have a Payslip linked to the Payrun.\nComputing payroll should use the employee’s applicable contract and selected salary structure.\nPayslips should show understandable components such as Basic, Allowances, Deductions, Gross, and Net Salary.\nPayroll issues, such as missing required information or duplicate payslips, should be visible to the user.\n\n\nPayroll Workflow:\n\nThe intended flow is broadly:\n\nDraft → Compute → Validate → Mark Paid\n\nPaid/finalised payroll should remain available as historical data.\n\n\nSalary Structures & Salary Rules:\n\nA Salary Structure contains the rules used to calculate salary.\nSalary Rules can represent Basic Salary, Allowances, Deductions, Gross, Net, etc.\nRules should be processed according to their sequence.\nDifferent calculation methods may be supported, such as fixed amounts, percentages, or formulas.\n\nParticipants are free to design the calculation engine as long as salary rules actually drive Payslip calculations.\n\n\nPayslip PDF:\n\nUsers should be able to generate/print a Payslip showing the employee’s payroll calculation for that period.\nSending Payslips can also be supported from the Payrun.\n\n\nPayroll Dashboard:\n\nThe dashboard should use actual data created through the HR and Payroll flows rather than hardcoded values.\n\nIt should provide useful payroll/HR insights such as:\n\nSalary totals\nPayslip status\nSalary by department\nSalary trends\nAttendance overview\nTime Off overview\nPayroll warnings or items requiring attention\n\nFilters such as Period, Department, Employee Type, or Company should affect the relevant dashboard data.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
